    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="1607" n="1567" xml:id="pg1567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/5–2754: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 828<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Israel</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d828-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-27T17:51:00-04:00">May 27, 1954—5:51
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>818. UK Embassy reports French have decided join US–UK <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >démarche</hi> to Israel and Jordan re border measures and have urged two
                    tactical moves: (1) that Israel Government be informed of fact of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> Amman re border measures and prospective
                    similar approach Israel this subject; (2) that reaction UNSYG be sought on
                    measures UN could implement unilaterally. UK
                    Foreign Office has agreed these moves and instructed UK missions Tel Aviv and
                    New York proceed accordingly.</p>
                <p>Embassy should indicate to UK and French Embassies Tel Aviv that US associates
                    itself with UK–French advising Israel Government per (1) above with earnest hope
                        IG will keep matter confidential.</p>
                <p>USUN will be advised shortly re joining in
                    UK–French approach UNSYG per (2) above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d828-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d828-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to New York; repeated to Amman, London, Paris, and Jerusalem; sent by
                    air pouch to Ankara, Baghdad, Beirut, Cairo, Damascus, Jidda, and Rome.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
